    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0731" n="607" xml:id="pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2259: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-01T17:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 1—3:46
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>325. My September 24th, 4 p.m. Foreign Office now state that further inquiries
                    elicit that one Japanese is interested in the matter but that he is not likely
                    to succeed as he has not the support or countenance of the Japanese Government.
                    Also that the Japanese military authorities have nothing to do with the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s no. 165, September 27. Japanese Foreign Office has no
                    information concerning such negotiations and have never heard of them according
                    to the statement by the Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <p>Have informed Stevens.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d584-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d584-f1" n="42" xml:id="d584-f1-content">
                <p>Last two paragraphs paraphrased.</p>
